# CHANGELOG

## 0.3.2

- `Endpoint.gate` exposes the endpoint permission gate explicitly
  (`"public"` | `"logged"` | list of permission names | `None` when not
  configured), without collapsing it the way `Endpoint.permissions` does.
- Template rejection now propagates: `Flow2Code.code()` returns a bool, `main()`
  exits non-zero when any module was rejected, and `TemplateBase.report_errors()`
  is the handled-error channel (stderr + `self.errors`).

## 0.3.0

- Added support for the new LiWE Flow 2 in SvelteJS
